              "bbox": [
                0.252,
                0.473,
                0.746,
                0.543
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_table_10.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>x</td><td>16</td><td>12</td><td></td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td>y</td><td>9</td><td></td><td>48</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.564,
            0.845,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 20 workers take 4 days to complete laying a road. How many days will 10 workers take to complete laying the same length of road?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.607,
            0.846,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we decrease the number of workers, then the number of days to complete the work will increase by the same factor. So these quantities are inversely proportional. So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X_{1}y_{1}=X_{2}y_{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.675,
            0.212,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.674,
            0.539,
            0.697
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "20 \\times 4 = 10 \\times y_{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.71,
            0.564,
            0.738
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "y_{2} = \\frac{20 \\times 4}{10} = 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.751,
            0.687,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It will take 8 days for 10 workers to complete the work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.782,
            0.847,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We notice that when the number of workers halved, the number of days to complete the work doubled. Quantities are inversely proportional if, when one quantity changes by a factor n, the other quantity changes by the inverse "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { n }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
